| Command                  | What it does                                                        |
|--------------------------|---------------------------------------------------------------------|
| `dude docs`              | Serve `docs/` via MkDocs Material in dev mode at http://localhost:8001 |
| `dude docs --port 9000`  | Same, on a custom port                                              |

Docs are live-reload: edit any `.md` file under `docs/docs/` and the browser refreshes automatically.

### Project-local custom commands

This project can define its own `dude` commands under `.dude/commands/`. Each
file becomes a command named after the file (`reset.ts` → `dude reset`); no
registration step. They appear in `dude help` under **PROJECT COMMANDS** and
take precedence over stack commands of the same name (so a `.dude/commands/up.ts`
overrides the default `dude up`). The core commands `init`, `upgrade`, `version`,
and `help` are reserved.

Commands are loaded with [jiti](https://github.com/unjs/jiti), so they can be
written in TypeScript and `import` any package added to the project. Use the
`defineCommand` helper for type-checking:

```ts
// .dude/commands/reset.ts
import { defineCommand } from '@cubocicloide/dude'

export default defineCommand({
  description: 'Reset the database to a clean state.',
  args: { force: { type: 'boolean', description: 'Skip confirmation.' } },
  async run({ projectRoot, args }) {
    // ...
  },
})
```

See `.dude/commands/README.md` (shipped with the scaffold) for the full contract.

