## Claude AI assistance

This project ships a set of Claude skills and agents inside `.claude/`.
Invoke skills from the Claude chat panel with `/skill-name`.

### Skills (slash commands)

| Skill | What it does |
|-------|--------------|
| `/security-scan` | Full SAST scan → parallel fix agents per finding → PR + Jira issues |
| `/verify-security-fixes` | Re-scan, confirm resolved findings, close Jira issues, update baseline |
| `/fix-issues` | Fetch open Jira issues → route to `issue-fixer` or `security-fixer` agents → PR |
| `/create-jira-issue` | Guided Jira issue creation with type/priority/labels |
| `/clean-branches` | Prune merged and stale local/remote branches |
| `/draft-email` | Draft a professional email from a brief |

### Agents (autonomous workers)

| Agent | What it does |
|-------|--------------|
| `issue-fixer` | Implements a single Jira issue in its own git worktree; opens PR; transitions issue to Done |
| `security-fixer` | Fixes a single SAST finding in its own worktree; handles suppressions and CVE updates |

Agents run in isolated git worktrees (one branch per task) and can operate in
parallel when orchestrated by `/fix-issues` or `/security-scan`.

### Saved config (autodiscovery)

Skills read Atlassian/Bitbucket connection details from `.claude/config.json`
(gitignored). Create it on first use:

```json
{
  "jira": { "projectKey": "PROJ" },
  "bitbucket": { "workspace": "my-org", "repo": "{{projectName}}" }
}
```

